<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28582" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">membrānŭla</span></b> , ae,
			f.
		dim.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				little skin</i> or <i>membrane.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">membranula, quae sub cute calvariam cingit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels. 8,
					4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oculi,</span>”
				<i>membrane of the eye</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					7, 7, 13</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A parchment</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">iisque imperes, ut sumant membranulam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 4, 4</span></i>
			, b, 1.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Plur., an instrument</i> or <i>document written on parchment</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quae membranulis meā manu scriptis
					continebuntur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					32, 102</span></i>
			 prooem.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
